00:08:16.440 --> 00:08:18.288
And mine was also very much,

00:08:18.288 --> 00:08:22.614
basically my entire decision to
get my MBA was around leadership.

00:08:22.614 --> 00:08:26.474
But I will highlight three dimensions
of it that I think were important for

00:08:26.474 --> 00:08:27.917
me in making the decision.

00:08:27.917 --> 00:08:31.256
So the first is that, I wanted
a place that was going to force and

00:08:31.256 --> 00:08:35.678
push me to self-reflect and think about
what are my own strengths and weaknesses.

00:08:35.678 --> 00:08:39.659
And what's going to help give me both
a toolkit to do that self-reflection and

00:08:39.659 --> 00:08:43.542
then take that feedback and learn those
things about myself and apply them.

00:08:43.542 --> 00:08:47.880
And actually have that sort of
really pragmatic aspect to it.

00:08:47.880 --> 00:08:49.813
The second reason which
is more aspirational,

00:08:49.813 --> 00:08:51.270
and people kind of touched on this.

00:08:51.270 --> 00:08:55.704
But I have a really important boss in my
work experience who had actually gone

00:08:55.704 --> 00:08:59.860
to Stanford and had been an Arbuckle
fellow and a whole bunch of things,

00:08:59.860 --> 00:09:04.106
who I think it's still probably
the single greatest mentor that I have.

00:09:04.106 --> 00:09:09.391
And is the first person I go to to bounce
decisions off of and ideas off of.

00:09:09.391 --> 00:09:12.674
And she was really good in I think both
determining kind of when to give me

00:09:12.674 --> 00:09:13.823
the warm hug approach and

00:09:13.823 --> 00:09:16.689
when to give me a little bit
more of a butt-kicking approach.

00:09:16.689 --> 00:09:20.150
And just understanding that there's
a whole array of tools that matter.

00:09:20.150 --> 00:09:24.494
And kind of knowing a person really deeply
and being the person that I turn to.

00:09:24.494 --> 00:09:28.614
And so, I wanted to be able to add one of
my biggest aspirations career-wise is to

00:09:28.614 --> 00:09:32.263
be able to pay that forward and to be
able to do that same to other people.

00:09:32.263 --> 00:09:34.088
And so that was a big piece of it.

00:09:34.088 --> 00:09:37.816
And then the third and final thing is
that, I actually come from an industry

00:09:37.816 --> 00:09:40.373
